# Baseline hardening for the static React bundle. `_headers` is part of the
# static-assets contract, so these rules apply identically in `wrangler dev`
# and in production. The Worker adds the same headers (plus a request id) to
# every `/api/*` response and to the SPA shell.
#
# Content-Security-Policy is deliberately left out for now: the SPA ships no
# inline scripts, but enabling CSP safely needs a nonce/hash pipeline and an
# end-to-end review of every asset loader, so it stays a documented follow-up.
#
# This file cannot vary by host, so `x-frame-options: SAMEORIGIN` is stripped
# from the local build only: the sandbox live preview embeds the app in an
# iframe served from another origin, and a document with SAMEORIGIN cannot be
# framed there. `scripts/dev.mjs` removes the line from `dist/client/_headers`
# after the build; the deployed file keeps it.
#
# Note: `_headers` must not be served as a file itself; Cloudflare consumes it
# at deploy time.
/*
  x-content-type-options: nosniff
  referrer-policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  permissions-policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

/index.html
  cache-control: no-cache

/assets/*
  cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
